==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|loup|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*laubą}}, perhaps from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*leup-||peel, break off}}. Compare Low German {{term|Loov|lang=nds}}, Dutch {{term|loof|lang=nl}}, English {{term|leaf|lang=en}}, Danish {{term|løv|lang=da}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/laʊ̯p/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Laub.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}
* {{rhymes|aʊ̯p|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|n|Laubes|gen2=Laubs|-}}

# [[foliage]], [[greenery]], [[leaves]] {{qualifier|on a tree or fallen onto the ground, but particularly the latter}}
#: ''grünes Laub''
#: ''fallendes Laub''
#* Hans Wollschläger, ''Von Sternen und Schnuppen: bei Gelegenheit einiger Bücher'', volume 1, page 209:
#*: Sie [die Orangen] hängen eben tatsächlich mitten im grünen '''Laub''' gelb an den Bäumen.

